Finish the two-page migration: prove it, flip it, retire the legacy path. We do not patch the legacy two-page path. We finish the new one, prove it, make it the default, and retire the old one. Phase 1 — the proof: cross-sheet drag selection and copy; focus/tab order; IME; editing churn across a sheet boundary and at a page break with caret and viewport holding; performance on the 115-page synthetic and sample02, before vs after the flip, no regression past noise. Fail-before recorded. Phase 2 — the flip and the retirement: the PageSheet path becomes the only pages-mode path, the env flag and #if DEBUG gate go away, multiContainerSpreadEnabled ceases to exist; the legacy container code is removed unless something still depends on it — name every dependent and propose the cut line; behaviour parity table. Code Director lock after a Vibe Check I approve; budget by hand; every claim a failing-before test or a measurement.